<h3>RSPL Help Page</h3>
<p>Recommended Spare Part List : The recommended parts are classified in 4 groups: P (parts for preventive maintenance), M (parts for maintenance), 0 (parts for overhaul), and C (critical parts). </p>
<h4>-P- Group: Scheduled Maintenance parts</h4>
<p>This group will show the part required for the schedule maintenance and need of course to be consistent with the maintenance chart of the unit.</p>
<p>The qty shown in the P column will correspond to the quantity needed for 1 unit and for 2 years, or 2000 operating hours if the main engine of the unit is under 50KW or 3000 operating hours if main engine of the unit is above 50KW)</p>
<h4>-M- Group: Wear and Tears parts.</h4>
<p>This group will show all the parts and quantity needed to accomplish the maintenance of 1 up to 3 identical equipments, and shall typically contains: spare wheels, belt, brake pads, MDW, FTC , some hoses, wiper blade, GPU cable and coupling, bulbs, fuses, wheel nut and studs, seal kits, rubber mount, muffler, sender, sensors….</p>
<h4>-0- Group: Overhaul Parts</h4>
<p>This group will show all the parts and quantity needed to accomplish major maintenance on the equipments, and shall typically contains: callipers, pin and bushing, brake drums, etc. A lot of “0” parts, will appear in the “M” column, but qty shall be adjusted for 1 units overhaul maintenance in the “O” column.</p>
<h4>-C- critical part.</h4>
<p>It is related to parts, which aren’t suppose to fail during normal operations, but may. These parts are critical for the equipment and will ground the unit in case of failure, and are justified in the customer inventory if he operates a significant fleet of equipment. The typical components shown in this column can be: garos box, plc board for loaders, A/C controller for Electric bag tractor, main hydraulic pump, starter motor for engines, alternators…</p>

